ng industry as well the life of the fishermen, their families and the coastal culture through the centuries.","wpu":"Westfjords Heritage Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Westfjords_Heritage_Museum_445.jpg/960px-Westfjords_Heritage_Museum_445.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ósvör Maritime Museum","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":66.1505,"lo":-23.214944,"d":9321,"ds":"The Ósvör Maritime Museum is a museum in Bolungarvík, Westfjords, Iceland.","wpu":"Ósvör Maritime Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Bolungarvik_02.jpg/960px-Bolungarvik_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Ísafjörður is a town in the northwest of Iceland. The oldest part of Ísafjörður with the town centre is located on a spit of sand, or eyri, in Skutulsfjörður, a fjord which meets the waters of the larger fjord Ísafjarðardjúp. With a population of about 2,600, Ísafjörður is the largest settlement in the peninsula of Vestfirðir (Westfjords) and the administration centre of the Ísafjarðarbær municipality, which includes—besides Ísafjörður—the nearby villages of Hnífsdalur, Flateyri, Suðureyri, and Þingeyri.","wpu":"Ísafjörður"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}